  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Jeffrey Springs gave Detroit everything early, and the game was done before anyone pretended it might not be.",
    "what_this_means": "Detroit broke through in the second inning and added three more in the fifth. The Athletics got one run across nine innings on one sacrifice fly. A single moment of contact in 12 strikeouts and 7 hits that never threatened to matter. Joshua Kuroda-Grauer went 3-for-4, the only evidence the lineup could make contact, but the other eight names in the order logged nine of those strikeouts. The bullpen. Sterner, Barnett, Suarez. Threw clean innings after Springs exited, but by then Detroit had already decided the game. This is what happens when one pitcher falls apart in the wrong inning and the offense has nothing to answer with. Kuroda-Grauer was the only light. Nobody else showed up.",
